From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Timur=20Krist=C3=B3f?= <timur.kristof@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 01:11:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] radv/nir: Don't fold constant offset into index VGPR for VS
 inputs anymore
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

On GFX6-7, use the SGPR offset to achieve correct bounds
checking behaviour, because the constant offset is included
in the bounds checking.

On GFX8+, just use the constant offset as-is because it
is not part of the bounds check.

With this commit, the code can also be simplified because
now each VS input load can be represented with just a single
memory load instruction and we don't need to split them here
anymore on GFX6-7.

We can also remove the attribute index offset and stride.
These are no longer needed because the index VGPR will
now always be just the actual vertex or instance index.

Cc: mesa-stable
Signed-off-by: Timur Kristóf <timur.kristof@gmail.com>
Reviewed-by: Rhys Perry <pendingchaos02@gmail.com>
Acked-by: Marek Olšák <maraeo@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit e27bfacb4720c6a50be0eaf648532a70593888f4)

Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/44168>
(cherry picked from commit cb711f671cd4bc8db7c6d0fa7d158a9a68897186)
